$DIR/main.p:18:2: cannot store o in package variable keep, which outlives v
    o points into v. v is a local variable of direct (declared at main.p:14).
    When direct returns, v's memory is reclaimed, but package variables live for
    the whole program, so package variable keep would be left pointing at
    reclaimed memory.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Store values instead of views of v, or allocate v and store its owner, an
    owned[pluto/vec.Vec[int]], which moves there:
        keep = new(pluto/vec.Vec[int])
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3002" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:28:2: cannot store p in package variable keep, which outlives v
    p points into v. v is a local variable of moved (declared at main.p:23).
    When moved returns, v's memory is reclaimed, but package variables live for
    the whole program, so package variable keep would be left pointing at
    reclaimed memory.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Store values instead of views of v, or allocate v and store its owner, an
    owned[pluto/vec.Vec[int]], which moves there:
        keep = new(pluto/vec.Vec[int])
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3002" for a longer explanation)
